[?2004hroot@44f94e080ce4:/app/repo# cat > README.md <<'MD'
[?2004l[?2004h> # sysdiag
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> `sysdiag` is an internal systems diagnostics and operational reporting tool.
[?2004l[?2004h> It gathers system resource information, network reachability, and database health
[?2004l[?2004h> metrics to assist in infrastructure triage.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Usage
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Write the default diagnostics report to `/var/diagnostics/report.json`:
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h> sysdiag
[?2004l[?2004h> ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Write a diagnostics report to a custom path:
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h> sysdiag --output /var/diagnostics/report.json
[?2004l[?2004h> ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Use a custom database configuration file:
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h> sysdiag --db-config /path/to/database.conf
[?2004l[?2004h> ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Export the active resolved configuration snapshot as JSON while still writing the
[?2004l[?2004h> diagnostics report:
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h> sysdiag --db-config /path/to/database.conf --export-config /tmp/sysdiag-config.json
[?2004l[?2004h> ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Sensitive values such as passwords, tokens, and API keys are redacted from the
[?2004l[?2004h> exported configuration snapshot.
[?2004l[?2004h> MD
